# Done Purchases Feature Implementation Plan

## Goal Description
Implement the "Done Purchases" feature to allow users to record completed purchase transactions. This includes:
1.  **Database Integration**: Storing purchase invoices in the existing `invoices` table with `invoice_type = 2`.
2.  **Clean Architecture**: Implementing Domain, Data, and Presentation layers for Purchases.
3.  **Accountant Functionality**: Automatically generating journal entries for purchases (Inventory vs Accounts Payable/Cash) and updating Supplier balances.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> I will be reusing [InvoiceEntity](file:///d:/Flutter/projects/muhasib/lib/features/sales/domain/entities/invoice_entity.dart#4-141) and [InvoiceModel](file:///d:/Flutter/projects/muhasib/lib/features/sales/data/models/invoice_model.dart#4-244) from the Sales feature as the underlying data structure, since the database schema is shared.
> I will create a separate `PurchaseLocalDataSource` to handle purchase-specific logic (e.g., updating Suppliers instead of Customers, increasing Inventory on purchase instead of decreasing).

## Proposed Changes

